ncrement with no closing criterion), neither the program nor the change is written, but the\n      stored document remains, attached to a change id no record names.\n    what_expected: >\n      A refused trajectory leaves nothing behind, or what it leaves is named by the refusal.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Run `/495 adopt` on a trajectory whose global requirement no increment carries, no milestone verifies and no scope decision sets aside.\"\n      - \"The adoption is refused, no program or change exists, and the object store holds the document under the unused change id.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The artifact is stored before the kernel decides, and nothing removes or names it after a refusal.\n    evidence: >\n      Named by the automated arbitration of e10s04 from its acceptance run (dossiers c2 and c4); the order of operations is\n      read in `harness.ts` (`artifacts.store` of the trajectory before `commitProgram`).\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Store the document only once the kernel has accepted the program, or record the refusal with the document it read.\n    status: open\n50618a2 docs: the registry no longer lists as open a survey whose analyser report was cut or increments naming gaps without a cited survey, both refused at adoption\neb7a2ee docs: register that a survey whose analyser report was cut at 1000 findings undercounts or omits the gaps a trajectory adopts\nf47c0b0 docs: register that increments naming gaps are adopted unchecked when the trajectory cites no survey","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"342ba2e5-f9e8-42ad-b928-e6443387bc63","uuid":"7c5b19f0-7fd7-4569-aa0e-95974934b917","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:51:32.605Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"bugs:\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-27T170100\n    date: \"2026-09-27\"\n    title: \"G1 accepts a mandatory requirement's satisfied_by_reference claim without evidence, before G2/G5 are known to catch a false one\"\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p